From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maicon Alves <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:49:42 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 02/13] OpenGL: draw indexed 2D batches with glDrawElements

drawElements() used glDrawRangeElements, which OpenGL ES 2.0 doesn't
have (it came with ES 3.0). On a real ES 2.0 context (Mesa lima on a
Mali-400, or llvmpipe with MESA_GLES_VERSION_OVERRIDE=2.0) the call
fails with GL_INVALID_OPERATION and draws nothing. That is every
draw2DImageBatch(), so all text: menus come up with no labels at all.
glDrawElements draws the same thing; the range is only a hint.

Upstream: not sent yet; master still calls glDrawRangeElements there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/irr/src/OpenGL/Driver.cpp b/irr/src/OpenGL/Driver.cpp
index b2d3e067d..12179df56 100644
--- a/irr/src/OpenGL/Driver.cpp
+++ b/irr/src/OpenGL/Driver.cpp
@@ -996,7 +996,7 @@ void COpenGL3DriverBase::drawArrays(GLenum primitiveType, const VertexType &vert
 void COpenGL3DriverBase::drawElements(GLenum primitiveType, const VertexType &vertexType, const void *vertices, int vertexCount, const u16 *indices, int indexCount)
 {
 	beginDraw(vertexType, reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(vertices));
-	GL.DrawRangeElements(primitiveType, 0, vertexCount - 1, indexCount, GL_UNSIGNED_SHORT, indices);
+	GL.DrawElements(primitiveType, indexCount, GL_UNSIGNED_SHORT, indices);
 	endDraw(vertexType);
 }
 
